From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:18:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/18] Define SOMAXCONN_HINT where winsock2.h lacks it

mingw-w64 does not have the Windows SDK's macro.

Upstream: not submitted; mingw-w64 could add the macro
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/java.base/windows/native/libnio/ch/Net.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/java.base/windows/native/libnio/ch/Net.c b/src/java.base/windows/native/libnio/ch/Net.c
index 6c07ca8fc..04a26d6fd 100644
--- a/src/java.base/windows/native/libnio/ch/Net.c
+++ b/src/java.base/windows/native/libnio/ch/Net.c
@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@
  * Definitions to allow for building with older SDK include files.
  */
 
+#ifndef SOMAXCONN_HINT
+#define SOMAXCONN_HINT(b) (-(b))
+#endif
+
 #ifndef MCAST_BLOCK_SOURCE
 
 #define MCAST_BLOCK_SOURCE          43
